      "side": 1,
      "message": "Returning early here makes the code harder to follow and isn\u0027t doing anything useful, because this is just creating ninja rules.  If you fail to generate a rule use ctx.ModuleErrorf().  Nothing else cares at runtime if the rule was generated, so you can just keep generating the rest of the rules until something checks ctx.Failed(), stops calling GenerateBuildActions for new modules, and reports the errors to the user.",
